mfd: max77705: accept the PASS2 revision

max77705_i2c_probe() refuses any chip whose PMICREV revision field is
not PASS3. The Samsung Galaxy Tab S8+ (SM-X800) carries a MAX77705 that
reads PMICID1 0x15 and PMICREV 0x02: PASS2. Samsung's own driver for
this board maps ID 0x15 revision 2 to "MD15 PASS2" and runs the chip
with the same top-level setup (interrupt source and mask registers,
MAINCTRL1 active discharge) that this driver performs, so accept PASS2
alongside PASS3. Other revisions are still rejected.

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
index e98c76d6b..2e9b81f26 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ static int max77705_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	pmic_rev = pmic_rev_value & MAX77705_REVISION_MASK;
-	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
+	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS2 && pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "Rev.0x%x is not tested\n", pmic_rev);
 
 	/* Active Discharge Enable */
